    "8": {
      "reviewed": true,
      "translation": "They say that the world is unreal, without foundation, without a Lord, and born from one another; what else could be its cause? They say that desire alone is its cause. Śrīdhara explains that they reject the authority of the Vedas and the Lord as creator and orderer, and regard sexual desire as the only cause of the world’s flow.",
